An L-shaped room has all right angles. Its total height is $300\text{ cm}$ and its upper section is $150\text{ cm}$ wide. The lower section extends $7\text{ m}$ beyond the upper section and is $2\text{ m}$ high. Find the floor area in $\text{m}^2$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (0,0)--(8.5,0)--(8.5,2)--(1.5,2)--(1.5,3)--(0,3)--cycle;
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$300\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (0.75,3) {$150\text{ cm}$};
\node[above] at (5,2) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8.5,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

workedExamples.solution_text:
Use metres for all lengths: $300\text{ cm}=3\text{ m}$ and $150\text{ cm}=1.5\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\draw (0,0)--(8.5,0)--(8.5,2)--(1.5,2)--(1.5,3)--(0,3)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (1.5,0)--(1.5,2);
\node at (0.75,1.5) {$A_1$};
\node at (5,1) {$A_2$};
\node[left] at (0,1.5) {$3\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (0.75,3) {$1.5\text{ m}$};
\node[above] at (5,2) {$7\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8.5,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
The first rectangle covers the full height.
$\begin{align*} A_1&=1.5\times3\\ &=4.5\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
The lower extension is a separate rectangle.
$\begin{align*} A_2&=7\times2\\ &=14\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
$\begin{align*} A&=A_1+A_2\\ &=4.5+14\\ &=18.5\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$

