workedExamples.question_text:
Find each remaining area.
(a) A wall is $8\text{ m}$ long and $3\text{ m}$ high. Three separate square windows, each with side $1\text{ m}$, are cut out.
(b) Four identical corner squares are removed from a square of side $10\text{ m}$. Each removed square has side $2\text{ m}$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw (2,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(10,2)--(10,8)--(8,8)--(8,10)--(2,10)--(2,8)--(0,8)--(0,2)--(2,2)--cycle;
\draw[thin] (0,2)--(0,-1.3);
\draw[thin] (10,2)--(10,-1.3);
\draw[<->] (0,-1)--(10,-1) node[midway,below] {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (8,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
All angles in (b) are right angles.

workedExamples.solution_text:
(a) Subtract the areas of all three windows.
$\begin{align*} A&=8\times3-3\times(1\times1)\\ &=24-3\\ &=21\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$
(b) Complete the surrounding square, then subtract all four corner squares.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.45]
\draw (2,0)--(8,0)--(8,2)--(10,2)--(10,8)--(8,8)--(8,10)--(2,10)--(2,8)--(0,8)--(0,2)--(2,2)--cycle;
\draw[dashed] (0,2)--(0,0)--(2,0);
\draw[dashed] (8,0)--(10,0)--(10,2);
\draw[dashed] (10,8)--(10,10)--(8,10);
\draw[dashed] (2,10)--(0,10)--(0,8);
\draw[thin] (0,10)--(0,11.3);
\draw[thin] (10,10)--(10,11.3);
\draw[<->] (0,11)--(10,11) node[midway,above] {$10\text{ m}$};
\node[right] at (10,1) {$2\text{ m}$};
\node[below] at (9,0) {$2\text{ m}$};
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
$\begin{align*} A&=10\times10-4\times(2\times2)\\ &=100-4\times4\\ &=100-16\\ &=84\text{ m}^2 \end{align*}$

